%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2989f6b7554baf142b3f807ffa71cecf, type: 3}
  m_Name: TutorialEntriesContainer
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  tutorialEntries:
  - id: 0
    tutorialEntryText: '<b>Confidential Document</b>

      

      <b>Conductor</b>,

      

      If
      you are reading this document, it means you have been assigned to duty aboard
      an <b>Interworld Train</b>.

      So not ask why it is you.

      Do not
      ask where this train is truly headed.


      Your role has been clearly defined..


      <b>Guard
      the Harmony.</b>

      <b>Maintain order.</b>

      <b>Ensure that every
      soul reaches where it is meant to go.</b>

      

      The train under your
      care is a <b>Bridge</b>.

      It connects the world of the viking with what
      lies beyond.

      Not all passengers are aware that their journey has already
      ended.'
  - id: 1
    tutorialEntryText: 'You are <b>the Conductor</b>.


      Not a judge.

      Not
      a savior.

      Not an executioner.

      

      Your task is not to pass
      judgement upon the deeds of the passengers, but to <b>enforce the rules of
      passage</b>.

      Yet remember - every decision you make affects the delicate
      balance of the Train and yourself.

      

      <b>Keep in mind - Rules
      exist so that the Train may continue its journey.</b>'
  - id: 2
    tutorialEntryText: "During each shift you will:\r\n    - walk between the carriages
      of the Train,\r\n    - speak with travelers,\r\n    - inspect their tickets
      and Life Cards,\n\r\nEach passenger must be verified for:\n    - ticket validity,\r\n   
      - consistency of name and personal data,\r\n    - date of passage,\r\n    -
      and any other detected anomalies.\n\n<b>Remember!</b>\nSome tickets are issued
      incorrectly. Others may have long expired. There are also passengers who should
      never have boarded the Train at all.\r\n<b>All anomalies will be reported to
      your superiors.</b>"
  - id: 3
    tutorialEntryText: "<b>The Train operates through Harmony.</b>\n\nEvery decision
      you make influences the level of Harmony. And the level of Harmony determines
      the condition of the Train.\nWhen Harmony weakens:\r\n    - lights may begin
      to flicker,\r\n    - sounds may fade or distort,\r\n    - your own memories
      may begin to blur.\n\nThe Train observes.\r\nThe Train remembers.\n\r\nToo
      many deviations from the rules may lead to <b>Loss of Harmony</b>.\nAnd then
      - the journey may come to an end."
  - id: 4
    tutorialEntryText: "<b>Every shift leaves a mark.</b>\n\nTo occupy your thoughts,
      our Dear Employee, we have provided you with a <b>Conductor\u2019s Journal</b>.\nYou
      may record your thoughts, reflections, and memories within it.\r\nUse it freely,
      it is yours alone. It will not be reviewed..\n\n\n\n<b>Final note,</b>\n\r\nNot
      every story deserves to continue.\r\nNot every soul is ready to reach its destination.\r\n\nYour
      task is not to mend the world.\r\nYour task is to keep the Train moving.\r\n\n<b>Guard
      the Harmony</b>.\r\n<b>And do not ask too many questions</b>."
